<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations> a owl:Ontology;
    rdfs:comment "The post-trade operations module provides a semantic core for settlement, settlement reconciliation, and selected corporate-action servicing. Simple DvP/FoP settlement, direct non-transferable rights subscription, due-bill entitlement transfer, strict zero-tolerance reconciliation, and run-level digest/probe/closure reproducibility evidence are optional profiles rather than universal post-trade semantics. Confirmation, affirmation, clearing, CCP novation, and netting are out of scope here and are exposed only as traceability hooks on settlement instructions. The module characterizes cash and security flows around and after trade completion, including the entitlement economics that span the ex-date / settlement-window boundary, rather than only post-completion flows.";
    rdfs:label "Post-Trade Operations";
    owl:imports <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/foundation>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/instruments>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-data>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-rules>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/market-structure>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/orders-execution>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/portfolio-positions>, <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta>;
    owl:versionIRI <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/1.1.0>.
fin-post-trade:AbsenceProofKind a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "The absence-proof kind is a closed classification of a missing-side assertion as deterministic side absence, unknown coverage, or incomplete source coverage, used for distinguishing a proven business absence from a no-result query whose coverage is unknown.";
    rdfs:label "Absence Proof Kind";
    owl:oneOf _:l_d0c1bebdc6a25be47e28a0fc_0.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/scheme> a skos:ConceptScheme;
    skos:prefLabel "Absence Proof Kind";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/value/deterministicSideAbsence> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-post-trade:AbsenceProofKind;
    rdfs:comment "a completed universe probe proves the side is absent; required by the strict profile";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/scheme>;
    skos:notation "deterministicSideAbsence";
    skos:prefLabel "Deterministic side absence";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/value/incompleteSourceCoverage> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-post-trade:AbsenceProofKind;
    rdfs:comment "the query returned no rows and source coverage is provably incomplete";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/scheme>;
    skos:notation "incompleteSourceCoverage";
    skos:prefLabel "Incomplete source coverage";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
<https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/value/unknownCoverage> a owl:NamedIndividual, skos:Concept, fin-post-trade:AbsenceProofKind;
    rdfs:comment "the query returned no rows but source coverage is unknown";
    skos:inScheme <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/finance/post-trade-operations/AbsenceProofKind/scheme>;
    skos:notation "unknownCoverage";
    skos:prefLabel "Unknown coverage";
    <https://axiolune.ai/ontology/meta/core/annotations/sourceEvidenceRef> <https://axiolune.ai/references/axiolune-m2-controlled-vocabularies>.
fin-post-trade:CorporateActionAdjustment a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "The corporate action adjustment is a normalized post-evidence cash or security adjustment summary for one event and entitlement, used for summarizing completed asset-movement results but never itself serving as proof that assets moved.";
    rdfs:label "Corporate Action Adjustment";
